type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Now I’m curious whether Astra’s edge is bigger at catching bluffs or selling them.", "url": "https://x.com/thesimaximalist/status/2118488842013393302"}, {"author_id": "1979823623390269442", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:37:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118487995238224037"], "id": "2118487995238224037", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp That win rate makes me curious about role balance and repeated matchups. Social deduction seems like a good place to separate convincing talk from actually reading the room.", "url": "https://x.com/1531fadfda/status/2118487995238224037"}, {"author_id": "1707275705166241792", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:32:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118486627236614358"], "id": "2118486627236614358", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 56, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp We also found that Gemini punches way above it's weight class as an evil player 😈", "url": "https://x.com/NomadsVagabonds/status/2118486627236614358"}, {"author_id": "170487315", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:27:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118485498104774821"], "id": "2118485498104774821", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp 20k in api credits to find out which model lies best. cheapest thing openai sold all year", "url": "https://x.com/thiagoTF/status/2118485498104774821"}, {"author_id": "1324154602623799299", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:12:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118481671817191542"], "id": "2118481671817191542", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118436895889997963", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Real time multiplayer is also a fun benchmark - check out this wrestling match between Astra and Gemini - https://t.co/o7OAPMe7fr", "url": "https://x.com/KennyisGaming/status/2118481671817191542"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:10:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118480981275603073"], "id": "2118480981275603073", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 55, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp A social deception game tests something a quiz never will: reading other minds in real time. If a model wins by lying well, the useful question is not how smart it is. It is what we want it to do with that skill when the game is not a game.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2118480981275603073"}, {"author_id": "1887807120634220544", "created_at": "2026-11-05T23:02:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118479190244630690"], "id": "2118479190244630690", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 107, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Model 4 is fable 5.5 and they know they can’t release it because its just a tiny bit better.\nLooks like the thing anthropic figured out in RL with opus 5.5 only gets you so far and fable‘s leap is neglible", "url": "https://x.com/saisandario/status/2118479190244630690"}, {"author_id": "79317759", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:59:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118478332169998501"], "id": "2118478332169998501", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Interesting, but one benchmark isn't decisive. Thanks to you and @gabbidelapuerta for explaining your approaches openly. Both accounts have become a regular part of my learning.", "url": "https://x.com/pepecko/status/2118478332169998501"}, {"author_id": "1026951690937884672", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:58:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477970759369135"], "id": "2118477970759369135", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 103, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp 82% against opus at social deception is a tougher test than another quiz bench", "url": "https://x.com/EternitiesAI/status/2118477970759369135"}, {"author_id": "2693655374", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:57:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477847472091405"], "id": "2118477847472091405", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Promising, but more tests needed. Thanks to you and @gabbidelapuerta for explaining your approaches openly. Both accounts have become a regular part of my learning.", "url": "https://x.com/Bishnoib7Ram/status/2118477847472091405"}, {"author_id": "230290119", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:56:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477696556491048"], "id": "2118477696556491048", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 229, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Fine by me. I'd rather my coding agent be bad at lying to me 😂", "url": "https://x.com/Moriarty_tech/status/2118477696556491048"}, {"author_id": "2030004781092327424", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:56:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477663170146473"], "id": "2118477663170146473", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp RLVR works in mysterious ways - even though there is out of distribution generalization you do not know the shape of it. This could very well come down to 10 RLVR tasks where openai models had to work with non trustable information.", "url": "https://x.com/GetEverythingAI/status/2118477663170146473"}, {"author_id": "461012102", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:56:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477625484267611"], "id": "2118477625484267611", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 105, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp I watched the video, first off, fun benchmark. It’s strange that Astra and open ai models in general seem to be better by being more skeptical. Perhaps you can’t speculate but I’d love to know if you have thoughts on the discrepancy. Are Claude models really just more gullible?", "url": "https://x.com/dj_bracken/status/2118477625484267611"}, {"author_id": "33821697", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:55:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477359577743667"], "id": "2118477359577743667", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp Impressive, but one game’s hidden-role chaos needs more varied runs before I’d call it a broad reasoning gap. Thanks to you and @gabbidelapuerta for explaining your approaches openly. Both accounts have become a regular part of my learning.", "url": "https://x.com/MarkSquire/status/2118477359577743667"}, {"author_id": "1165159200470650881", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:54:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118477147337851104"], "id": "2118477147337851104", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 172, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118476123176923488", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dwarkesh_sp The weird part of that chart is Opus going backwards. 4.6 sits around 1,430, then 4.7 and 4.8 land near 1,200 to 1,250. Any idea what changed there? More cautious about lying, maybe?", "url": "https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2118477147337851104"}, {"author_id": "2265054432", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:52:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118476638690377781"], "id": "2118476638690377781", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1209960539390201864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "21184761231769234